I thought this might happen today.

258
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:15,100
Ross, I know the holidays can be rough...

259
00:14:15,350 --> 00:14:18,480
and it's probably really hard for you to be alone right now.

260
00:14:18,690 --> 00:14:19,810
You're alone.

261
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,020
No, I live with Phoebe.

262
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:26,190
I mean, you're alone-alone.

263
00:14:27,110 --> 00:14:31,160
And it's just not the time for us. I'm sorry.

264
00:14:31,950 --> 00:14:34,700
Oh, well. Can't blame a guy for trying.

265
00:14:39,370 --> 00:14:41,920
And, uh, if anyone needs help pretending to like it...

266
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:46,170
I learned some things in acting class. Try, uh, rubbing your stomach.

267
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:50,340
Or, uh, saying "Mm."

268
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,840
And, uh, oh, smiling.

269
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,220
Okay?

270
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:57,850
Yeah, I'm not gonna pay for those acting classes anymore.

271
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:03,060
Rachel, there you are. Let's serve that dessert already.

272
00:15:03,310 --> 00:15:07,440
Joey, you have to stop rushing me. You know what? You don't get any dessert.

273
00:15:07,690 --> 00:15:08,740
Really?

274
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:13,280
No, just kidding. I would never do that to you.

275
00:15:13,530 --> 00:15:16,330
Okay, everybody, it's trifle time.

276
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:20,200
So, now, Rach, this is a traditional English trifle, isn't it?

277
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:21,710
It sure is.

278
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:21,710
Wow.

279
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,040
So did you make it with beef or eggplant?

280
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:27,920
Beef.

281
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:27,920
I can't have any. I don't eat meat. Oh.

282
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:29,960
Aw.

283
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:34,640
Monica, I want you to have the first taste.

284
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:36,470
Really?

285
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,640
Wait, you only got whipped cream.

286
00:15:41,890 --> 00:15:44,060
You gotta take a bite with all the layers.

287
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,900
Okay.

288
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:49,690
You dropped a pea.

289
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:00,620
Well?

290
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:03,290
Mm.

291
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:11,760
It's good.

292
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,880
Really? How good?

293
00:16:14,090 --> 00:16:16,090
It's so good that I feel really selfish...

294
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:18,550
about being the only one who's eating it.

295
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:22,310
I think we should have everyone taste how good it is.

296
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:24,600
Especially Ross.

297
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:28,980
Mm-hm.

298
00:16:29,230 --> 00:16:31,190
Mm.

299
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:35,070
Yeah. This is so good that I'm gonna go enjoy it on the balcony.

300
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:41,200
So that I can enjoy the view whilst I enjoy my dessert.

301
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:44,460
I've gotta call my friend...

302
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:47,330
and tell her how good this is from Monica's room.

303
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:48,840
I'll help you dial.

304
00:16:51,590 --> 00:16:53,420
I'm gonna go into the bathroom...

305
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:56,630
so I can look at it in the mirror as I eat it.

306
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:01,560
Okay, what was that all about? Does it not taste good?

307
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,020
Let me try it.

308
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,020
No, no.

309
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:10,690
All gone.

310
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,440
So good.

311
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,780
Maybe Chandler has some left.

312
00:17:20,530 --> 00:17:22,580
It tastes like feet.

313
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,330
I like it.

314
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:30,960
Are you kidding?

315
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,760
What's not to like? Custard, good.

316
00:17:34,010 --> 00:17:37,180
Jam, good. Meat, good.

317
00:17:39,550 --> 00:17:43,010
So a bird just grabbed it...

318
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:48,440
and then tried to fly away with it...

319
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:51,270
and then just dropped it on the street?

320
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,990
Yes, but, if it's any consolation, before the bird dropped it...

321
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,280
he seemed to enjoy it.

322
00:17:59,990 --> 00:18:01,030
Rachel, come here.

323
00:18:01,870 --> 00:18:02,910
Okay.

324
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:06,660
I was just taking my Thanksgiving nap and I had another dream about Jack.

325
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:09,920
Phoebe, do I want to hear this?

326
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:09,920
I don't know, let's see.

327
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,290
Okay, I dreamt we were getting married...

328
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,550
and he left because he had to go fight a fire.

329
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:20,130
And, um, so, okay, I went to a nightclub and I saw him making out with a girl.

330
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:23,220
Oh, my God, he dream-cheated on you.

331
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,560
Yeah. But then Jacques Cousteau came...

332
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:28,100
and he kicked his ass for betraying me.

333
00:18:28,350 --> 00:18:29,980
It was so cool.

334
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:33,520
Then he took me diving and introduced me to his pet sea horse...

335
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:38,150
who was coming on to me. And, please, that is not gonna happen.

336
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:44,080
Boy, I'm glad I wore the big belt today.

337
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:49,540
Five minutes ago, a line like that would have floored me.

338
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:53,750
But now, nothing. Well, not nothing. I am still a woman.

339
00:18:57,130 --> 00:18:59,090
Ross? Let's go.

340
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:01,840
Oh, yeah. About telling Mom and Dad...

341
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:04,890
I was thinking about maybe writing a letter.

342
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:07,310
You know what? That's it. You've had your chance.

343
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,850
what?

344
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:12,770
Mom, Dad. Ross smoked pot in college.

345
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:14,610
What?

346
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:14,610
What?

347
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:17,280
You are such a tattletale.

348
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:22,490
Mom, Dad, heh...

349
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:25,620
you remember that time you walked in my room...

350
00:19:25,870 --> 00:19:27,700
and smelled marijuana?

351
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,450
Yes.

352
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,450
Yes.

353
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,210
I told you it was Chandler...

354
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:38,800
who was smoking the pot but...

355
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:43,130
it was me. I'm sorry.

356
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,680
It was you?

357
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,560
And, Dad, you know that mailman that you got fired?

358
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:51,480
He didn't steal your Playboys. Ross did.

359
00:19:56,360 --> 00:20:00,230
Well, Hurricane Gloria didn't break the porch swing. Monica did.

360
00:20:02,950 --> 00:20:05,530
Ross hasn't worked at the museum for a year.

361
00:20:06,990 --> 00:20:09,870
Monica and Chandler are living together!

362
00:20:12,830 --> 00:20:16,880
Ross married Rachel in Vegas. And got divorced. Again!

363
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,710
I love Jacques Cousteau.

364
00:20:23,470 --> 00:20:27,550
I wasn't supposed to put beef in the trifle.

365
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,470
I want to go!

366
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:37,610
That's a lot of information to get in 30 seconds.

367
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:42,030
All right. Joey, if you want to leave, just leave.

368
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:48,030
Rachel, no, you weren't supposed to put beef in the trifle.

369
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:50,240
It did not taste good.

370
00:20:52,870 --> 00:20:54,910
Phoebe, I'm sorry...

371
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:58,420
but I think Jacques Cousteau is dead.

372
00:20:59,630 --> 00:21:02,840
Monica, why you felt you had to hide the fact...

373
00:21:03,050 --> 00:21:05,930
that you're in an important relationship is beyond me.

374
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:09,050
And we kind of figured about the porch swing.

375
00:21:11,010 --> 00:21:12,140
Ross.

376
00:21:12,350 --> 00:21:13,470
Drugs?

377
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,690
Divorced again?

378
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:18,690
What happened, son?

379
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:23,860
I... I, uh... I got tricked into all those things.

380
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:30,120
Chandler, you've been Ross' best friend all these years...

381
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:33,160
stuck by him during the drug problems...

382
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:38,290
and now you've taken on Monica as well.

383
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:41,750
Well, I don't know what to say.

384
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:43,880
You're a wonderful human being.

385
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:48,470
Thank you.

386
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:48,470
No.

387
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,510
Thank you.

388
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:56,810
Monica and Ross, I don't know what I'm gonna do about the two of you.

389
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,730
I'll talk to them.

390
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:07,320
You guys, it was bananas...

391
00:22:07,570 --> 00:22:09,910
cream and beef.

392
00:22:10,740 --> 00:22:14,620
I just cannot believe that you ate that so that I wouldn't feel bad.

393
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:18,080
Well, actually, I didn't eat mine. It's still in the bathroom.

394
00:22:18,290 --> 00:22:19,290
No it isn't, I ate that.

395
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:24,130
And we left ours in Monica's bedroom.

396
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:26,630
Nope, got it and got yours too.

